/*! 
 * @defgroup flash
 * @ingroup mod_flash Flash Memory (Flash)
 * @brief Embedded flash memory controller for program storage and data persistence.
 * 
 * @details The Flash driver provides a hardware abstraction layer for the EFM
 *          (Embedded Flash Module) peripheral, enabling erase, program, and
 *          verification operations on internal flash memory. It supports both
 *          P-Flash (program flash) and D-Flash (data flash) regions, with
 *          optional NVR (Non-Volatile Region) access, boot swap, and HCU
 *          security key loading on supported devices.
 *
 * @section flash_features Key Features
 *
 * - **Multi-region support**: P-Flash, D-Flash, and NVR regions
 * - **Two operation modes**:
 *   - Synchronous (blocking): API returns after command completion
 *   - Asynchronous (interrupt-driven): API returns immediately; callback on completion
 * - **Sector, block, and array-level erase** granularity
 * - **Hardware read-after-write verification** (optional)
 * - **Quick erase with retry** for improved reliability
 * - **Data integrity**: 32-bit byte-sum checksum computation
 * - **ECC fault detection**: Single-bit (recoverable) and double-bit (unrecoverable) fault interrupts
 * - **Boot swap**: Dual-bank firmware update support
 * - **Security key loading**: AES/RSA key transfer to hardware crypto unit (HCU)
 * - **Callback support**: User-defined callbacks for async events and sync polling
 *
 * @section flash_memory_regions Supported Memory Regions
 *
 * | Region    | Description                       | Typical Use Case             |
 * |-----------|-----------------------------------|------------------------------|
 * | P-Flash   | Program Flash (main code storage) | Application firmware         |
 * | D-Flash   | Data Flash (persistent storage)   | Calibration, configuration   |
 * | NVR       | Non-Volatile Region               | Keys, serial numbers, trim   |
 * | Boot NVR  | Boot-swap control area            | Dual-bank update management  |
 *
 * @section flash_arch Module Architecture
 *
 * The Flash driver is organized into two layers:
 *
 * @verbatim
 *   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐
 *   │  Application                             │
 *   ├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
 *   │  Flash Driver  (flash_driver.h/c)        │
 *   │  └─ FLASH_DRV_* APIs                     │
 *   ├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
 *   │  HW Access     (flash_hw_access.h)       │
 *   │  └─ FLASH_Get/Set/Clear* inline fns      │
 *   ├──────────────────────────────────────────┤
 *   │  EFM Peripheral Hardware                 │
 *   └──────────────────────────────────────────┘
 * @endverbatim
 *
 * - **Flash Driver**: Application-level API with instance management, state
 *   tracking, sync/async mode handling, command sequencing, and callback dispatch.
 * - **HW Access Layer**: Thin inline wrappers for direct register reads/writes.
 *   Used only by the driver layer — not intended for application use.
 *
 * @section flash_config Configuration Parameters
 *
 * All configuration is carried in the flash_user_config_t structure:
 *
 * | Parameter    | Type             | Description                                           | Default   |
 * |--------------|------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|-----------|
 * | async        | bool             | true = interrupt-driven mode (RWW devices only)       | false     |
 * | disGlobalInt | bool             | true = suppress global IRQs during sync operations    | true      |
 * | readVerify   | bool             | true = HW read-verify after every erase/program       | true      |
 * | wdgEnable    | bool             | true = enable EFM watchdog (device-specific)          | false     |
 * | callback     | flash_callback_t | User event callback pointer or NULL_CALLBACK          | NULL      |
 *
 * @section flash_usage Usage Patterns
 *
 * @subsection flash_usage_basic Pattern 1 — Basic Init + Sector Erase + Program
 *
 * @code{.c}
 *   flash_user_config_t flashConfig;
 *   flash_state_t flashState;
 *
 *   // 1. Get defaults and initialize
 *   FLASH_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&flashConfig);
 *   FLASH_DRV_Init(0U, &flashConfig, &flashState);
 *
 *   // 2. Erase a 4 KB sector
 *   FLASH_DRV_EraseSector(0U, 0x00010000U, 4096U);
 *
 *   // 3. Program 256 bytes (64 words)
 *   uint32_t buffer[64] = { ... };
 *   FLASH_DRV_Program(0U, 0x00010000U, 256U, buffer);
 *
 *   // 4. Verify
 *   uint32_t checksum;
 *   FLASH_DRV_CheckSum(0U, 0x00010000U, 256U, &checksum);
 *
 *   // 5. Clean up
 *   FLASH_DRV_Deinit(0U);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection flash_usage_async Pattern 2 — Asynchronous Mode with Callback
 *
 * @code{.c}
 *   void flashCallback(flash_event_t event)
 *   {
 *       switch (event)
 *       {
 *           case FLASH_EVENT_COMPLETE:
 *               // Erase/program finished
 *               break;
 *           case FLASH_EVENT_ERROR:
 *               // Handle error
 *               break;
 *           default:
 *               break;
 *       }
 *   }
 *
 *   flash_user_config_t flashConfig;
 *   flash_state_t flashState;
 *
 *   FLASH_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&flashConfig);
 *   flashConfig.async = true;
 *   flashConfig.callback = flashCallback;
 *   FLASH_DRV_Init(0U, &flashConfig, &flashState);
 *
 *   // Erase returns immediately; callback is invoked on completion
 *   FLASH_DRV_EraseSector(0U, 0x00010000U, 4096U);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection flash_usage_nvr Pattern 3 — NVR Operations
 *
 * @code{.c}
 *   // NVR erase + program (available when FEATURE_EFM_ERASE_NVR_CMD_CODE is defined)
 *   FLASH_DRV_EraseNVR(0U, FEATURE_EFM_BOOT_NVR_ADDR);
 *
 *   uint32_t nvrData[4] = { 0x11223344, 0x55667788, 0x99AABBCC, 0xDDEEFF00 };
 *   FLASH_DRV_ProgramNVR(0U, FEATURE_EFM_BOOT_NVR_ADDR, 16U, nvrData);
 *
 *   uint32_t readBack[4];
 *   FLASH_DRV_ReadNVR(0U, FEATURE_EFM_BOOT_NVR_ADDR, 16U, readBack);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection flash_usage_bootswap Pattern 4 — Boot Swap
 *
 * @code{.c}
 *   // Swap boot blocks (available when FEATURE_EFM_BOOT_SWAP_CMD_CODE is defined)
 *   status_t status = FLASH_DRV_BootSwap(0U);
 *   if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
 *   {
 *       // Swap command accepted; takes effect on next reset
 *       NVIC_SystemReset();
 *   }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section flash_api API Quick Reference
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_Init() | Initialize driver with configuration. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_Deinit() | De-initialize and release resources. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() | Fill configuration struct with defaults. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_config Runtime Configuration
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_SetAsyncMode() | Switch between synchronous and asynchronous mode. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_SetDisableGlobalInt() | Toggle global IRQ suppression in sync mode. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_SetReadVerify() | Toggle hardware read verification after erase/program. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_erase Erase Operations
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_EraseArray() | Erase the entire flash array. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_EraseBlock() | Erase a flash block. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_EraseSector() | Erase one or more sectors. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_EraseSectorQuick() | Quick erase with automatic retry. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_program Program Operations
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_Program() | Program P-Flash or D-Flash region. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_ProgramDFlash() | Program D-Flash region only. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_integrity Data Integrity
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_CheckSum() | Compute 32-bit byte-sum checksum over a flash region. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_status Status Query
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_GetBusyStatus() | Check whether the driver is busy with an operation. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_GetDoneStatus() | Check the hardware command-done flag. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_GetReadCollisionFlag() | Check the read-collision error flag. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_irq Interrupt Management
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_EnableCmdCompleteInterrupt() | Enable command-done interrupt. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_DisableCmdCompleteInterrupt() | Disable command-done interrupt. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_EnableReadCollisionInterrupt() | Enable read-collision interrupt. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_DisableReadCollisionInterrupt() | Disable read-collision interrupt. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_EnableSingleBitFaultInterrupt() | Enable single-bit ECC fault interrupt. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_DisableSingleBitFaultInterrupt() | Disable single-bit ECC fault interrupt. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_EnableDoubleBitFaultInterrupt() | Enable double-bit ECC fault interrupt. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_DisableDoubleBitFaultInterrupt() | Disable double-bit ECC fault interrupt. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_nvr NVR Operations
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_EraseNVR() | Erase one NVR sector. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_ProgramNVR() | Program data to an NVR sector. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_ReadNVR() | Read data from an NVR region. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_bootswap Boot Swap
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_BootSwap() | Swap the active and inactive boot flash blocks. |
 *
 * @subsection flash_api_keys Security Keys
 * | Function | Description |
 * |----------|-------------|
 * | FLASH_DRV_LoadAESKey() | Load an AES key from NVR into the HCU. |
 * | FLASH_DRV_LoadRSAKey() | Load an RSA key from NVR into the HCU. |
 *
 * @section flash_notes Important Notes
 *
 * - **RAM-resident code**: The command write sequence (FLASH_LaunchCommandSequence)
 *   is executed from RAM. The linker must allocate a RAM section for this function
 *   using START/END_FUNCTION_DEFINITION_RAMSECTION macros.
 * - **Read-While-Write (RWW)**: Async mode is only supported on devices with RWW
 *   flash. On non-RWW devices, use synchronous mode only.
 * - **Flash command unlock**: The EFM peripheral requires an unlock sequence
 *   before each command. The driver handles this automatically.
 * - **Alignment requirements**: All destination addresses must be aligned to
 *   FEATURE_EFM_WRITE_UNIT_SIZE. Data buffers must be 32-bit aligned.
 * - **Callback restrictions**: Functions reachable from the callback must NOT
 *   reside in the flash block being erased or programmed. Place callbacks in RAM
 *   or in a separate flash block.
 * - **Clock dependency**: The EFM peripheral clock must be enabled via the
 *   clock_manager before calling any flash API.
 *
 * @section flash_integration Integration Guide
 *
 * To use the Flash driver in a project:
 *
 * 1. **Include headers**:
 *    @code{.c}
 *    #include "flash_driver.h"
 *    @endcode
 *
 * 2. **Clock setup**: Ensure the EFM clock is enabled before calling any API.
 *
 * 3. **Allocate state**: Declare a flash_state_t variable per instance;
 *    it must persist for the driver's lifetime.
 *
 * 4. **Interrupt setup** (async mode only): The EFM IRQ is automatically
 *    enabled by FLASH_DRV_Init() when async mode is selected.
 *
 * 5. **Linker configuration**: Map the RAM section for the command write
 *    sequence function.
 */
